<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 7 February, from 457 to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">457 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,569 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leo I crowned Eastern Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Backed by the powerful general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aspar">Aspar</a>, Leo I became emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. He is often said to be the first emperor crowned by the Patriarch, and he reigned until 474.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1301 CE <span class="tih-ago">725 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward of Caernarfon becomes the first English Prince of Wales</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward I invested his son, the future Edward II, with the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> after his conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. The title has been given to the heir to the English and British throne ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1792 CE <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Austria and Prussia ally against Revolutionary France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The two German powers signed a defensive alliance amid fears of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. War broke out that April, beginning more than two decades of conflict across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1812 CE <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Strongest of the New Madrid earthquakes strikes the Mississippi valley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last and largest of a series of great earthquakes hit near New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, Missouri. It created waterfalls and made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> briefly run backwards near the epicentre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1904 CE <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Great Baltimore Fire begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A fire broke out in a dry-goods warehouse and burned for some 30 hours, destroying more than 1,500 buildings in central Baltimore. Fire crews from other cities could not connect hoses to local hydrants.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1962 CE <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US embargo on trade with Cuba takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A proclamation by John F. Kennedy banning almost all imports from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> came into force. Extended since, it is one of the longest-lasting trade embargoes in modern history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1984 CE <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bruce McCandless makes the first untethered spacewalk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Using a nitrogen-jet backpack, the Manned Maneuvering Unit, McCandless flew about 100 metres from the shuttle Challenger. The photograph of him alone above Earth became famous.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1990 CE <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Communist Party agrees to give up its monopoly on power</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Central Committee accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a>'s proposal to end the party's constitutional leading role. The change opened the way to multi-party politics in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
